{
  "name": "huchen",
  "_about": "SCULPTED (2026-11-21, tools/creaturegen/rework/fish/salmonids.py): a huchen (Danube salmon), 1 m -- LONG and nearly ROUND in section, a torpedo; a broad flat-topped head, the big mouth reaching back behind the small eye; a small dorsal mid-back, the salmonid's little ADIPOSE fin before the tail, low pectorals, pelvics under the dorsal, a shallow-forked tail; copper-red flanks (its spawning dress) under a grey-green back, sprinkled with small dark spots above and on the head (the coat pattern `trout`, only its black spots), a cream belly. Each fin is one membrane sheet. A SWIMMER (the fish's plumbing).",
